lecommunications data, so information on subscriptions has been widely available for most countries. This gives a general idea of access, but a more precise measure is the penetration rate - the share of households with access to telecommunications. During the past few years more information on information and communication technology use has become available from household and business surveys. Also important are data on actual use of telecommunications services. Ideally, statistics on telecommunications (and other information and communications technologies) should be compiled for all three measures: subscriptions, access, and use. The quality of data varies among reporting countries as a result of differences in regulations covering data provision and availability.\n\nDiscrepancies may also arise in cases where the end of a fiscal year differs from that used by ITU, which is the end of December of every year. A number of countries have fiscal years that end in March or June of every year.","unresolved":["NO_CURRENT_WORLD_STATE_INFERENCE","NO_CAUSALITY","NO_POLICY_CONCLUSION"]},"boundary":{"publicOnly":true,"personalFact":false,"privateWrite":false,"liveMarketFact":false,"forecast":false,"currentData":false,"signalThresholdEvaluated":false},"admission":{"state":"ARCHIVAL_CWA_SOURCE_BOUND","licenseVerified":true,"archival":true},"projectionVersion":"f4daf1eb7c6963aa40f16a1933bfc19bca14c4a582bd62d1babc64c655443ea1","dimensionIds":["environment"],"title":{"en":"Internet use (% population)","zh-Hans":"互联网使用人口比（%）"},"sourceObservationRef":"IT.NET.USER.ZS:IDN:2024"},{"observationId":"GC.REV.XGRT.GD.ZS:IDN:2025","subject":{"subjectId":"WORLD:COUNTRY:IDN","type":"COUNTRY","countryCode":"IDN","spatialLevel":"COUNTRY"},"observationClass":"MEASUREMENT","knowledgeState":"UNKNOWN","observedAt":"2025","retrievedAt":"2026-11-02T03:37:55.364989+00:00","sourceRefs":[{"id":"WDI:GC.REV.XGRT.GD.ZS","url":"https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country/MY;SG;ID/indicator/GC.REV.XGRT.GD.ZS?forma